दृ cl. 6. Ā. द्रिय॑ते (ep. also ˚ति), to respect, honour (Dhātup. xxviii, 118);
 occurring only with prep. आ cf. आ-√ दृ;
 Desid. दिदरिषते, Pāṇ. vii, 2, 75.

दॄ cl. 9. P. दृणाति Pot. -दृणीयात्, ŚBr.;
 cl. 2. P. 2. sg. Subj. द॑र्षि, 2. 3. sg. द॑र्त् impf. 2. sg. अदर्, RV. (pf. ददा॑र, [2. sg. ददरिथ, Pāṇ. vi, 4, 126, Sch.; 3. pl. दद्रुर् or ददरुर्, vii, 4, 12, Sch.] aor. अदरत् [Ved. अदारीत्] Pāṇ. iii, 1, 59, Sch.; Subj. P. दर्षसि, द॑र्षत्; Ā. दर्षते; Pot. ˚षीष्ट, RV.; Prec. दीर्यात्, Hariv. 15177)
to burst, break asunder, split open, RV.; Hariv. (cf. above);
to cause to burst, tear, rend, divide, RV.; MBh.; BhP. :
Pass. दीर्यते (˚ति, MBh.), p. दीर्यमाण and दीर्यत्;
 pf. दद्रे (ŚāṅkhŚr. xiv, 27, 2) to be split, break open, fall asunder, decay, Br.; MBh.; Suśr.; Kāv.;
to be dispersed or scattered (as an army), MBh.; R.;
to be frightened or afraid (also दरति), Dhātup. xix, 47 :
Caus. P. दरयति, to split, tear, break open, RV.;
 P. Ā. दारयति, ˚ते;
 aor. अददरत् (Pāṇ. vii, 4, 95) to tear asunder, divide by splitting or digging, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to scatter, disperse, MBh. :
Intens. P. द॑र्दर्ति or दा॑दर्ति;
 Impv. 2. sg. दादृहि॑;
 Subj. 3. sg. दर्दिरत्;
 impf. 2. 3. sg. अ॑दर्दर्, 3. pl. अदर्दिरुर् = Caus. RV.
